&  &  &  & (\\frac{1}{0}) &  & (\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{2}{0}) &  & (\\frac{2}{1}) &  & (\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  & (\\frac{3}{0}) &  & (\\frac{3}{1}) &  & (\\frac{3}{2}) &  & (\\frac{3}{3}) \\\\  &  &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $(\\frac{3}{1})$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So,\n\n$$\n(\\frac{3}{1})=(\\frac{2}{0})+(\\frac{2}{1})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $(\\frac{2}{0}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-69669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e0184ee9fb99cf69b6b5a911cab20cbe1339b88801e66c5a1a5e76334cd8ab5"} {"question" "q-69669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-69669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(\\frac{1}{0})"] ["math" "(\\frac{1}{1})"] ["math" "(\\frac{2}{0})"] ["math" "(\\frac{2}{1})"] ["math" "(\\frac{2}{2})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-69669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(\\frac{2}{0})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-113608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n\n$$\n(\\frac{6}{5})=[]+(\\frac{5}{5})\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-113608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $(\\frac{6}{5}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $6$ and position $5$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe location of $(\\frac{6}{5})$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{1}{0}) &  & (\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{2}{0}) &  & (\\frac{2}{1}) &  & (\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{3}{0}) &  & (\\frac{3}{1}) &  & (\\frac{3}{2}) &  & (\\frac{3}{3}) \\\\  &  &  &  & (\\frac{4}{0}) &  & (\\frac{4}{1}) &  & (\\frac{4}{2}) &  & (\\frac{4}{3}) &  & (\\frac{4}{4}) \\\\  &  &  & (\\frac{5}{0}) &  & (\\frac{5}{1}) &  & (\\frac{5}{2}) &  & (\\frac{5}{3}) &  & (\\frac{5}{4}) &  & (\\frac{5}{5}) \\\\  &  & (\\frac{6}{0}) &  & (\\frac{6}{1}) &  & (\\frac{6}{2}) &  & (\\frac{6}{3}) &  & (\\frac{6}{4}) &  & (\\frac{6}{5}) &  & (\\frac{6}{6}) \\\\  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $(\\frac{6}{5})$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So,\n\n$$\n(\\frac{6}{5})=(\\frac{5}{4})+(\\frac{5}{5})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $(\\frac{5}{4}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-113608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e0184ee9fb99cf69b6b5a911cab20cbe1339b88801e66c5a1a5e76334cd8ab5"} {"question" "q-113608" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-113608" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(\\frac{4}{3})"] ["math" "(\\frac{4}{4})"] ["math" "(\\frac{5}{4})"] ["math" "(\\frac{6}{4})"] ["math" "(\\frac{6}{6})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-113608" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(\\frac{5}{4})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-69722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n\n$$\n(\\frac{3}{2})=(\\frac{2}{1})+[]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-69722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $(\\frac{3}{2}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $3$ and position $2$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe location of $(\\frac{3}{2})$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{1}{0}) &  & (\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{2}{0}) &  & (\\frac{2}{1}) &  & (\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  & (\\frac{3}{0}) &  & (\\frac{3}{1}) &  & (\\frac{3}{2}) &  & (\\frac{3}{3}) \\\\  &  &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $(\\frac{3}{2})$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So,\n\n$$\n(\\frac{3}{2})=(\\frac{2}{1})+(\\frac{2}{2})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $(\\frac{2}{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-69722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e0184ee9fb99cf69b6b5a911cab20cbe1339b88801e66c5a1a5e76334cd8ab5"} {"question" "q-69722" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-69722" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(\\frac{1}{0})"] ["math" "(\\frac{1}{1})"] ["math" "(\\frac{2}{0})"] ["math" "(\\frac{2}{1})"] ["math" "(\\frac{2}{2})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-69722" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(\\frac{2}{2})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-113604" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n\n$$\n(\\frac{2}{1})=(\\frac{1}{0})+[]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-113604" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $(\\frac{2}{1}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $2$ and position $1$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe location of $(\\frac{2}{1})$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{1}{0}) &  & (\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{2}{0}) &  & (\\frac{2}{1}) &  & (\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $(\\frac{2}{1})$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So,\n\n$$\n(\\frac{2}{1})=(\\frac{1}{0})+(\\frac{1}{1})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $(\\frac{1}{1}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-113604" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e0184ee9fb99cf69b6b5a911cab20cbe1339b88801e66c5a1a5e76334cd8ab5"} {"question" "q-113604" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-113604" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(\\frac{0}{0})"] ["math" "(\\frac{1}{1})"] ["math" "(\\frac{2}{0})"] ["math" "(\\frac{2}{2})"] ["math" "(\\frac{3}{1})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-113604" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(\\frac{1}{1})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-113617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the value of $(\\frac{6}{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-113617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binomial coefficient $(\\frac{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\frac{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=6$ and $r=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{6}{2}) & =\\frac{6!}{(6-2)!\\cdot 2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4!}{4!\\cdot 2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{\\cancel{4!}\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{2} \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-113617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e0184ee9fb99cf69b6b5a911cab20cbe1339b88801e66c5a1a5e76334cd8ab5"} {"question" "q-113617" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-113617" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "30"] ["math" "45"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-113617" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-70311" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the value of $(\\frac{7}{3}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-70311" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binomial coefficient $(\\frac{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\frac{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=7$ and $r=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{7}{3}) & =\\frac{7!}{(7-3)!\\cdot 3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4!}{4!\\cdot 3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot \\cancel{6}\\cdot 5\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{\\cancel{4!}\\cdot \\cancel{6}} \\\\  & =7\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =35.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-70311" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e0184ee9fb99cf69b6b5a911cab20cbe1339b88801e66c5a1a5e76334cd8ab5"} {"question" "q-70311" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5185697440d3e9b5857af13fed04c485e119c1add725cb8db7e35a883b337de"} {"question" "q-70311" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "14"] ["math" "21"] ["math" "35"] ["math" "60"] ["m